  message: "CLOSED done, 2026-09-25 (P2 review, dev e4a47383ab). DONE-AND-NEVER-CLOSED. Fixed by two later commits:\n- 'process': 566a8eae5b (2026-09-10) \"fix(javascript): process and performance are runtime globals, not external\". JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS now carries \"process\" (js_ts.py:882).\n- `new WebSocket(...)` receivers: bf8e138dac (2026-09-03, INV-misup / WI-nasuf) \"every instance-method call emits an edge, and a constructed or declared receiver carries its module\".\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE on the production path, re-running the row's shape. a.js body:\n    process.send(m); process.on(\"message\", x => x); const ws = new WebSocket(\"ws://x\"); ws.send(m); console.log(m)\nFull survey, then `hypergumbo io-boundaries --format json`. Four chains, one per catalogued primitive:\n    ipc_recv  process.on      -> javascript:process:0-0:on:external_symbol\n    ipc_send  process.send    -> javascript:process:0-0:send:external_symbol\n    net_send  WebSocket.send  -> javascript:WebSocket:0-0:send:external_symbol\n    logging   console.log     (the positive control, as in the filed fixture)\nThe filed defect was \"emit NO edge despite being catalogued\"; each now emits a calls edge that reaches its catalogued boundary.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS has no OTHER drift. It is still hand-maintained, which is exactly what WI-nukub (open) is about."  # f3e5
